from scripts.curate_remaining import Batch
b=Batch('03-engineering',['Material Science','Ceramics Engineering','Metallurgy','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Structural Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Nuclear Engineering','Power Engineering','Chemical Engineering']);a=b.a;u=b.u
# Concrete component, manufacturing and evaluation routes, never eternal-performance promises.
a('MAS-06','ELE-07','A thermoelectric converter could be evaluated as one harvesting channel where an adequate temperature difference is available.','A high material figure of merit does not establish universal ambient power, total conversion efficiency or a maintained heat gradient.','enabling')
a('MAS-08','CIV-08','A protective, repairable surface could be tested for particular pavement cracking or weather-exposure modes.','A coating does not establish indefinite resistance to rutting, traffic wear and every climate.')
a('MAS-08','STR-10','A repairable protective layer could be one candidate defense against specified surface-exposure mechanisms.','No layer is assumed to prevent all corrosion, fatigue, fire or aging of every structural material.','enabling')
a('MAS-08','PWR-09','A qualified coating could be investigated for environmental protection of selected power-equipment surfaces.','Dielectric, magnetic and thermal aging remain separate; no zero-degradation material is established.')
a('CRM-04','MAS-03','A ceramic ionic conductor could be a candidate electrolyte route for the proposed lithium-metal battery.','Conductivity does not establish full-cell energy density, charging rate, cycle life or absolute safety.','enabling')
a('CRX-02','CRM-04','Structure prediction could help choose candidate ceramic compositions for conductivity and stability tests.','Structure prediction does not determine all transport, interface or manufacturing properties.')
a('CRM-02','MEC-05','A high-temperature ceramic repair process could provide a repair mechanism for appropriately designed hot load-bearing parts.','Crack closure in a ceramic would not establish diagnosis, topology reconfiguration or repair of arbitrary machines.','enabling')
a('MET-02','MEC-05','A metal crack-repair mechanism could provide a repair option for suitable structural parts.','Healing material does not supply whole-machine sensing, control or autonomous reconfiguration.','enabling')
a('CRM-07','STR-07','Complex ceramic printing could be a fabrication route for testing selected architectured structural elements.','Technical-ceramic printing does not establish meter-scale construction, common-material economics or structural performance.','enabling')
a('CRM-07','CRM-09','Geometric ceramic fabrication could provide candidate porous or channelled scaffold forms for biological tests.','Geometry and density do not establish vascularization, bone integration or tissue replacement.','enabling')
a('CRM-10','MEC-05','Reversible ceramic shape changes could provide an actuation option for a suitably designed high-temperature reconfiguring structure.','A material strain cycle does not establish a mechanical system’s repair, load path or lifetime.','enabling')
a('MET-01','MET-07','Composition and processing search could help screen candidate alloys against high-temperature strength and oxidation targets.','A predictive design engine is not a validated alloy and need not be universal to improve a particular design.')
a('MET-01','MET-10','Multi-property alloy search could help compare candidates for the proposed hardness, ductility and density combination.','No design method guarantees that the desired property combination exists.')
a('MET-01','NUC-07','Alloy-design calculations could help formulate candidates for molten-coolant compatibility testing.','Corrosion, mass transfer and irradiation behavior still need material-specific evidence.')
a('MET-02','MET-03','Repairing incipient damage could be tested as one way to reduce fatigue-crack growth in a qualified loading regime.','Healing cracks does not establish no initiation, infinite life or resistance to every cyclic load.')
a('MET-06','CIV-03','A suitable corrosion-resistant alloy could supply a metallic reinforcement route for testing.','Rebar cost, bond, strength and real exposure must be checked; absolute immunity is not established.','enabling')
a('MET-06','NUC-07','A candidate corrosion-resistant alloy could be investigated in a specified coolant chemistry.','Generic corrosion resistance cannot be transferred to irradiation-assisted corrosion or erosion by assumption.')
a('NUC-07','NUC-06','A molten- or liquid-cooled long-service design could use a qualified coolant-compatible material as one lifetime component.','Not every nuclear battery uses these coolants, and material endurance does not establish unattended operation.')
a('MET-09','IND-05','Restoring alloy properties through reuse could supply one material loop in a circular manufacturing proposal.','An alloy loop does not establish all-material recovery, energy closure or zero waste.','enabling')
a('MEC-01','MEC-04','Reducing qualified contact losses could improve the bearing or transmission portion of a mechanical-storage design.','Dry superlubricity does not eliminate every loss, standby decay or long-term degradation.')
a('MEC-08','MEC-02','Contact-state predictions could supply boundary and loading information for a candidate wear model.','A contact law does not itself predict all damage chemistry or wear transitions.','enabling')
a('MEC-02','MEC-05','Damage forecasts could help schedule or trigger a proposed repair and reconfiguration action.','Prediction alone does not provide a repair mechanism or guarantee exact remaining life.')
a('MEC-03','ROB-10','A mechanism-synthesis tool could generate linkage candidates for task-specific robot body design.','Linkage synthesis does not cover every embodiment or determine a globally optimal body.','enabling')
a('MEC-10','MEC-03','New movable topology families could expand the candidate mechanisms available to a synthesis search.','A new family does not solve arbitrary motion, force or manufacturability constraints.','enabling')
a('MEC-06','STR-01','A qualified isolation system could be one route to reducing a specified seismic excitation.','The full-band perfect isolation ambition is not assumed achievable or sufficient for zero damage.','alternative-route',group='seismic-protection')
a('MEC-09','ROB-03','Lower transmission losses could reduce one part of a robot’s task-energy budget.','Lossless transmission remains an aspiration and would not establish biological total efficiency.')
a('MEC-09','MEC-04','A qualified transmission could reduce losses during a mechanical store’s charging and discharge.','Transmission efficiency would not establish long-duration storage efficiency or eliminate all standby loss.')
a('MEC-05','CIV-05','Reconfiguring load-bearing mechanisms could provide one implementation route for adaptive structural elements.','Whole-system behavior, response time and safe load transfer remain independent.','enabling')
a('CIV-01','CIV-08','Concrete crack sealing could be tested for the cracking portion of a pavement-durability proposal.','Healing concrete does not establish resistance to all traffic, climate and binder failure modes.')
a('CIV-02','STR-03','Evolving concrete degradation states could be inputs to a proposed long-term structural response model.','Chemical durability does not determine every creep, shrinkage or steel fatigue response.','enabling')
a('STR-03','STR-09','Material-time response predictions could supply a component of a sensor-updated structural lifetime model.','Exact long-term material forecasts and exact failure prediction are not established.','enabling')
a('STR-09','CIV-02','Observed structural-state histories could provide checks for concrete-degradation predictions.','This is measurement-to-model feedback, not circular confirmation of either model.','feedback')
a('CIV-03','STR-10','A qualified reinforcement system could address a specified corrosion pathway in reinforced structures.','It would not establish eternal durability of all materials against every hazard.','enabling')
a('RHE-09','CIV-04','Particle-shape and friction models could contribute a candidate granular-flow description to a soil-response model.','Pore-pressure dynamics, cyclic history and a mitigation method remain separate.','enabling')
a('CIV-04','CIV-10','A soil-response and mitigation model could contribute to the seismic-ground component of coastal resilience analysis.','It does not establish protection against every coastal hazard or affordable centuries-long resilience.','enabling')
a('CIV-05','STR-01','Load-responsive structural properties could be investigated as an adaptive seismic-protection route.','No adaptation law or zero-damage guarantee is established.','alternative-route',group='seismic-protection')
a('STR-02','STR-01','A passive damping mechanism could be investigated as another seismic-response strategy.','Damping does not remove all structural and non-structural damage mechanisms. Approaches may combine.','alternative-route',group='seismic-protection')
a('STR-04','STR-01','A passive prestress or geometry response could be tested as a load-redistribution component under a specified earthquake input.','Passive adaptation does not establish zero damage for every structure and earthquake.')
a('CHE-09','CIV-06','A feedstock-accounting and recovery framework could help qualify waste inputs for a proposed concrete binder.','Material recovery does not establish binder strength, net carbon balance or large-scale supply.')
a('CIV-09','STR-07','A qualified robotic construction process could be a scale-up route for assembling architectured structural elements.','Fast construction does not prove the hierarchy’s mechanics, code compliance or zero waste.')
a('ROB-01','CIV-09','Object handling could be a component of an assembly-based construction route.','Building-scale loads, site tolerances and structural verification remain distinct; printing routes may not use this capability.','enabling')
a('STR-09','CIV-10','Sensor-updated failure scenarios could help evaluate and adapt a proposed multi-hazard design.','Prediction is not prevention, and no exact hazard forecast or resilience guarantee is implied.')
a('STR-06','IND-05','Recoverable framing components could supply a reuse loop for part of a building-material system.','Disassembly does not establish zero performance loss, all-material closure or energy closure.','enabling')
a('STR-08','ELE-07','A strain-to-electricity structural element could be explored as one environment-specific harvesting channel.','The source does not establish universal ambient supply or the target’s conversion threshold.','enabling')
a('STR-09','MEC-05','Failure-state estimates could help choose a response in a suitably instrumented adaptive load-bearing system.','A building-scale twin does not automatically transfer to every machine, and estimates do not supply repair actuators.')
a('IND-01','IND-04','A throughput and bottleneck model could provide part of a factory twin’s process dynamics.','A production theory does not establish a complete physical model or autonomous optimization.','enabling')
a('IND-02','IND-04','An exact scheduling solver, if realized, could provide candidate schedules for the twin’s controller.','The ambitious solver’s complexity claim is not validated; optimization does not establish execution or a complete twin.')
a('IND-03','IND-09','A model of human error could help test candidate socio-technical safeguards in defined tasks.','Predicting error does not make catastrophic error impossible in every system.')
a('IND-04','IND-08','A factory/supply model could help compare timing and coordination policies for reducing waiting and inventories.','No prediction model eliminates uncertainty or establishes globally bufferless production.')
a('IND-01','IND-08','A production-dynamics model could expose buffering and timing assumptions in a just-in-time proposal.','Its result may constrain rather than enable the zero-inventory aspiration.','enabling')
a('IND-07','SWE-10','A knowledge-work measurement model could help define comparisons between a coding agent and specified team workflows.','Such a comparison would not establish universal productivity laws or superiority on every engineering task.')
a('IND-10','IND-04','A multi-objective formulation could help state the trade-offs to be optimized in a proposed control policy.','Objectives and Pareto analysis do not establish a perfect twin or a single global social optimum.')
a('CHE-09','IND-05','A chemical recirculation model could supply one process-family loop for a broader industrial proposal.','A chemical loop cannot establish total industrial material or energy closure.','enabling')
a('IND-09','CHE-06','Explicit error-proofing primitives could inform a safety argument for an autonomous plant.','Human-error constraints do not cover all reaction, equipment and control hazards, and the universal safety claim remains unverified.')
a('NUC-02','NUC-10','A controllable fusion power source could be investigated as an electric-propulsion power route.','The source’s gain and conversion claims are not achieved facts; mass, heat rejection and thrust performance remain separate.','enabling')
a('MEC-04','PWR-04','A mechanical storage design could be investigated for a specified long-duration grid-storage duty.','Its zero-loss ambition does not establish the seasonal cost, capacity, footprint or efficiency target.','enabling')
a('CSC-08','PWR-10','A fault-tolerant coordination protocol could be a software component of a decentralized grid-control proposal.','Protocol agreement does not imply electrical stability or resilience to arbitrary disturbances.','enabling')
a('PWR-02','PWR-10','Grid-forming control could be an electrical-control component in an inverter-rich decentralized design.','Local controls do not establish grid-wide stability under every topology and disturbance.','enabling')
for id,reason in {
'MAS-05':'This complete cloak ambition overlaps OPT-01 and ELE-04; no independent component mechanism is identified between the complete targets.',
'MAS-09':'The catalyst/system scope overlaps CHM-05. A second artificial-photosynthesis ambition is not a prerequisite for the first.',
'MAS-10':'No specified ambient topological phase or qubit implementation connects these alternative phase possibilities to a definite device route.',
'CRM-01':'Ductility and hardness are material-property goals. No selected device or fabrication architecture here specifies a qualified use of that combination.',
'CRM-03':'Transparency and theoretical strength do not supply the dynamic optical or imaging functions in the collection; a complete optical design is missing.',
'CRM-05':'The original source flags equivalence to ELE-01. Retain the reference rather than a ceramic-to-superconductor causal arrow.',
'CRM-06':'A possible hot-air vehicle use needs a qualified thermal architecture, processing and loads. No such application mechanism has yet been justified in this batch.',
'CRM-08':'Coupling magnitude does not specify an energy-harvesting, memory or actuator implementation; translating it directly into power or computation would add an unsupported mechanism.',
'MET-04':'Bulk amorphous processing alone does not establish any listed structure’s complete property combination; no qualified part and load case was identified.',
'MET-05':'High elongation is not a construction or assembly process. No target part, strain path and retained-property argument justifies a downstream capability here.',
'MET-07':'A hot oxidizing-atmosphere alloy needs an application-specific load and fabrication route before an engine or propulsion capability can be inferred.',
'MET-08':'Single-crystal perfection alone does not establish the targeted hardness, corrosion or high-temperature property combinations in other alloy goals.',
'MET-10':'This proposed property combination lacks a specified component architecture; using it as a generic strong-materials hub would manufacture coverage.',
'MEC-07':'No qualified propulsor geometry, load regime or vehicle integration is specified by a downstream system reviewed in this batch.',
'CIV-07':'The target overlaps STR-05’s universal collapse-arrest ambition. Neither complete goal is a separate causal input to the other.',
'STR-05':'The source overlaps CIV-07’s collapse-prevention goal. Preserve both source entries without inventing a causal sequence.',
'IND-06':'No network mechanism is specified that guarantees continuity under arbitrary shocks without buffers or extra cost. Related optimization targets do not establish that guarantee.',
'NUC-03':'Transmutation completeness and a closed fuel cycle are different goals; no specified reactor/target process connects this universal waste-removal ambition to another complete system.',
'NUC-09':'No reviewed material-accounting, separation and safeguarding design establishes the stated no-weapons-usable-material architecture; waste transmutation alone would not suffice.',
'PWR-07':'The gigawatt, long-distance wireless system has no qualified source, propagation and receiver architecture in these entries. ELE-02 is an overlapping transfer ambition, not a prerequisite.',
'CHE-01':'Universal perfect separation at essentially zero energy requires a feasibility and process model before use as a component; a generic separation-to-every-plant arrow was rejected.'
}.items():u(id,reason,'source-equivalence' if id=='CRM-05' else 'unresolved-mechanism')
b.reject('CRM-06','MET-07','A ceramic oxidation barrier does not establish a coating-free alloy; the material requirements differ.')
b.reject('MAS-03','PWR-04','Electrolyte energy density alone does not establish seasonal storage economics, loss and lifetime.')
b.reject('NUC-03','NUC-09','Waste transmutation does not establish proliferation resistance of an entire fuel cycle.')
